  "recommendation": "Most promising onset improvement so far: a threshold flagging ~10% of healthy borrowers (set on validation) catches 33 of 73 onsets instead of 6, with precision 34%. Not deployed: validation had only 18 onsets and the test window was inspected before; confirm on fiscal-2026 outcomes first."
 },
 "findings": [
  "No experimental network beats the deployed one by a statistically clear margin on overall stress; the three-year GRU is +0.015 PR-AUC with an interval that includes zero.",
  "Training only on healthy borrowers made the networks worse, not better: 65 training onsets are too few.",
  "The deployed network already ranks new onsets about as well as the specialist models; its low onset recall comes from a single alert threshold set for a population where most stress is persistent.",
  "A separate watch-list threshold for healthy borrowers is the most promising next step (research only).",
  "The textbook scores (Altman Z'', Ohlson O) rank next-year stress clearly worse than the network: about 0.18 lower PR-AUC on the same rows, with intervals well below zero."
 ],
 "limitations": [
  "One held-out window (2021-25), inspected several times; no later outcomes yet.",
  "Accounting-stress proxy, not default; U.S. non-financial SEC filers with revenue of USD 50m or more.",
  "Onset results rest on 73 test onsets (65 in training, 18 in validation), so intervals are wide."
 ],
